ed obito just  had one of his eyes at the time while  kakashi had the other both eyes awakened  at the same time  both eyes can use kamui a space-time  ninjutsu  that lets the user transfer objects to  and from another dimension  obito's right eye is able to transfer  parts of the user's body or their entire  body  to the other dimension so that attacks  appear to simply pass through the user's  body  in this way obito's body can be  completely intangible  and as a result he can pass through  walls or even the ground  he can only keep his body completely  intangible for around  five minutes and he cannot teleport in  this state thus when he solidifies in  preparation for teleportation  he is vulnerable he can transfer himself  or others to the kamui dimension by  sucking them into his eye but it appears  like they have  to be close to him he can also enter the  kamui dimension and return to any  location he pleases  so in a way it's like an improved flying  thunder god technique  where you don't have to use pre-existing  marks the kamui dimension can store  weapons that obito could launch at  opponents or he could use the dimension  as a safe place to retreat to  since the only way to get there is by  using obito's eyes  people he transfers to that dimension  have no way out  unless they have access to one of his  eyes in contrast  the left eye has more of a long-range  focus  it can create a barrier space around an  object in the distance and teleport it  to the kamui dimension the object is  sucked into the barrier space  rather than into the eye when kakashi  first starts using it he tends to have  trouble with accuracy and often misses  his target he also has trouble creating  a big enough barrier space  however eventually he becomes skilled  enough to warp flying weapons and to  create large barriers  kakashi even figures out how to create  the barrier around himself  in doing so he can transport himself  into the kamui dimension  and thus also make use of tele